================================================================================
THE PIVOTAL MEASUREMENT
Does kata-agent execute createContainer hooks that arrive on a CDI spec found
INSIDE the guest?   Kata 4.1.0, guest kernel 6.18.35-nvkvm, 2026-08-28.
ANSWER: YES.  No patch to the Kata runtime, shim, agent or rustjail.
================================================================================

--- the setup -------------------------------------------------------------
The guest-side generator (/usr/local/bin/nvkvm-guest-cdi-gen, run from a
modprobe.d `install` directive when kata-agent modprobes nvkvm-guest) was made
to emit one extra field in /var/run/cdi/nvkvm.yaml:

  containerEdits:
    deviceNodes:
      - path: "/dev/nvidiactl"
      ...
    hooks:
      - hookName: createContainer
        path: /usr/local/bin/nvkvm-hook-probe
        args: ["nvkvm-hook-probe", "probe"]

/usr/local/bin/nvkvm-hook-probe touches a marker inside the container's rootfs:

  for c in /run/kata-containers/*/rootfs; do
    [ -d "$c" ] && touch "$c/NVKVM_HOOK_RAN"
  done

--- the run ---------------------------------------------------------------
$ docker run --runtime=nvkvm-kata -e VISIBLE_CDI_DEVICES=nvidia.com/gpu=0 \
      --rm ubuntu:24.04 sh -c "ls -l /NVKVM_HOOK_RAN 2>&1; ls /dev/nvidia* 2>&1"
-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 0 Aug 28 02:33 /NVKVM_HOOK_RAN
/dev/nvidia-uvm
/dev/nvidia-uvm-tools
/dev/nvidia0
/dev/nvidiactl
rc=0

The marker is INSIDE the container.  The hook ran, in the container's mount
namespace, after the rootfs was assembled and before pivot_root -- which is
exactly the contract `nvidia-cdi-hook update-ldcache` needs.

--- why this is the deciding measurement ----------------------------------
Host-injected hooks are deleted before the agent ever sees the spec:

  src/runtime/virtcontainers/kata_agent.go:1055  constrainGRPCSpec()
      // Disable Hooks since they have been handled on the host and there is
      // no reason to send them to the agent.
      grpcSpec.Hooks = nil

Guest-resident ones are not.  They arrive through handle_cdi_devices()
(src/agent/src/device/mod.rs), land in the container spec, and are executed by

  src/agent/rustjail/src/container.rs:621-632
      // CreateContainer Hooks:
      // before pivot_root after prestart, createruntime
      create_container_states.execute_hooks(hooks.create_container()..., state)

so docs/design/02-libraries-via-cdi.md sec D option 3 -- "regenerate the spec in
the guest ... UNVERIFIED: whether kata-agent actually executes hooks arriving
via the guest CDI path" -- is now VERIFIED, positively.

--- what the guest rootfs has to work with --------------------------------
(loop-mounted kata-nvkvm.image, Ubuntu 24.04 noble)
  chroot:   /sbin/chroot        present
  ldconfig: /sbin/ldconfig      present
  sh:       /bin/sh             present
  sed:      /bin/sed            present
